# Melee damage from the swing (#465, D-NEW): no charge - a hit's damage fraction (the aim ratio, 1 = the engine's fully
# charged strike) comes from the stroke's size and the speed of the blade's point that touched, the weaker of the two
# deciding: a touch outside a swing, or a stroke below a minimum, deals the minimum 0.1 (vr_melee_noswing=min, the
# default; none: nothing); a big and fast slash or lunge the full damage. The trigger, held long or short, changes
# nothing. Every hit logs melee.hit with aim, speed, size and kind.
#   .\scripts\dev\smoke-test.ps1 -Playground -VrSim idle -Sequence melee-damage
# The swings are ramps of the simulated right controller through the goblin (0.85 m): in 60 frames 1.3 m/s (no swing:
# a touch), in 24 frames 3.2 m/s at 90 Hz (part of the speed range), in 8 frames 9.6 m/s (above it). Where the blade
# first touches the goblin - so a stroke's size at contact - depends on the IK arm's reach and the goblin's mesh, so each
# factor is proven alone with the other one's range set live to "always full" (min = max = 0) or out of reach; the
# scale itself is MeleeSwingTest's. Damage has the engine's rolls (critical, armour class): the sequence asserts the
# aim. Swing hits (vr.melee.hits) and touches (vr.melee.touches) are counted apart; asserts on vr.melee.last follow a
# swing's end at once (a touch of the resting blade comes 0.6 s after a hit at the earliest). The goblin is respawned
# between the groups of hits.
@sim idle
@playground

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false
@assert area eq 30
# Free look closes the inventory a --loadlevel start keeps open (TRAPS.md, #394)
freelook on
@until vr.melee.refused ne inventory 5s

# One weapon per run (TRAPS.md): the dagger, recovery 0.6 s after a hit
inventory playeraddfromscene dagger_9001
dagger_9001.equip player
@until vr.melee.recovery.weapon eq dagger 5s
@assert vr.melee.active eq true
@assert vr.weapon.place eq hand
# The provisional defaults, set live: a cfg.ini kept from an earlier build keeps its old values (TRAPS.md); the
# defaults themselves are MeleeSwingTest::testContactAim's
melee noswing min
melee quality min
melee pathscale 1
melee slash dagger default
melee stab dagger default
@frames 2
@assert vr.melee.params.class eq dagger
@assert vr.melee.params.noSwing eq min
@assert vr.melee.params.quality eq min
@assert vr.melee.params.slash.pathMin eq 0.25
@assert vr.melee.params.slash.speedMax eq 5
@assert vr.melee.params.stab.pathMax eq 0.45

# The dagger level with the goblin's chest, the hand to the right - moved there slowly - then the peaceful goblin 60
# units ahead
vr-sim @+1-60 hand right pos 0.45 -0.8 -0.35
vr-sim head rot 0 -25 0
@frames 75
playground place 60
@frames 10
@assert playground.npcAlive eq true
@remember npc playground.npc
@assert vr.melee.swings eq 0
@assert vr.melee.hits eq 0

# 1. A slow touch: the dagger swept through the goblin at 1.3 m/s is no swing - and the goblin is peaceful: a touch
# reaches only an NPC that fights the player (the coordinator's decision, D-NEW), so nothing happens
@assert playground.npcFighting eq false
@remember touches vr.melee.touches
@mark
vr-sim @+1-60 hand right pos -0.4 -0.8 -0.35
@frames 75
@assert vr.melee.swings eq 0
@assert vr.melee.hits eq 0
@assert vr.melee.touches eq {touches}
@nolog melee\.hit source=player

# 2. With the defaults, a fast swing back: a swing hit with its measured speed and size in the log
@until vr.melee.recovery.left eq 0 5s
@remember hits vr.melee.hits
@mark
vr-sim @+1-8 hand right pos 0.45 -0.8 -0.35
@until vr.melee.swings ge 1 5s
@until vr.melee.swinging eq false 5s
@assert vr.melee.hits eq {hits+1}
@assert vr.melee.last.target eq {npc}
@assert vr.melee.last.swing gt 0
@assert vr.melee.last.aim ge 0.1
@assert vr.melee.last.speed gt 1.5
@log melee\.hit source=player target=goblin_base_\d+ .*aim=\d\.\d\d speed=\d+\.\d\d size=\d\.\d\d kind=slash

# 3. The speed alone (the size range set to always full): a medium swing part of the damage, a fast one the full
melee slash dagger 0 0 2 5
@until vr.melee.params.slash.pathMax eq 0 5s
@until vr.melee.recovery.left eq 0 5s
@remember hits vr.melee.hits
@mark
vr-sim @+1-24 hand right pos -0.4 -0.8 -0.35
@until vr.melee.hits ge {hits+1} 5s
@until vr.melee.swinging eq false 5s
@assert vr.melee.last.swing gt 0
@assert vr.melee.last.aim gt 0.1
@assert vr.melee.last.aim lt 0.95
@assert vr.melee.last.speed gt 2
@assert vr.melee.last.speed lt 5
@assert vr.melee.last.kind eq slash
@log melee\.hit source=player target=goblin_base_\d+ .*aim=0\.\d\d speed=[2-4]\.\d\d size=\S+ kind=slash
@until vr.melee.recovery.left eq 0 5s
@remember hits vr.melee.hits
@mark
vr-sim @+1-8 hand right pos 0.45 -0.8 -0.35
@until vr.melee.hits ge {hits+1} 5s
@until vr.melee.swinging eq false 5s
@assert vr.melee.last.aim ge 0.99
@log melee\.hit source=player target=goblin_base_\d+ .*aim=1\.00 speed=\S+ size=\S+ kind=slash
@remember full vr.melee.last.aim

# 4. The trigger changes nothing: held 2 s, the same fast swing deals the same; a medium swing with it held still deals
# part of the damage (the old charge made it full); a short press during a fast swing the same as without
playground kill
@until playground.npcAlive eq false 5s
playground pull respawn
@until playground.npcAlive eq true 5s
playground place 60
@mark
vr-sim action trigger right 1
@frames 180
@assert vr.melee.trigger eq true
@until vr.melee.recovery.left eq 0 5s
@remember hits vr.melee.hits
vr-sim @+1-8 hand right pos -0.4 -0.8 -0.35
@until vr.melee.hits ge {hits+1} 5s
@until vr.melee.swinging eq false 5s
@assert vr.melee.trigger eq true
@assert vr.melee.last.aim eq {full}
@until vr.melee.recovery.left eq 0 5s
@remember hits vr.melee.hits
vr-sim @+1-24 hand right pos 0.45 -0.8 -0.35
@until vr.melee.hits ge {hits+1} 5s
@until vr.melee.swinging eq false 5s
@assert vr.melee.last.aim gt 0.1
@assert vr.melee.last.aim lt 0.95
vr-sim action trigger right 0
@frames 10
@assert vr.melee.trigger eq false
@until vr.melee.recovery.left eq 0 5s
@remember hits vr.melee.hits
vr-sim action trigger right 1; vr-sim @+1-8 hand right pos -0.4 -0.8 -0.35; vr-sim @+5 action trigger right 0
@until vr.melee.hits ge {hits+1} 5s
@until vr.melee.swinging eq false 5s
@assert vr.melee.last.aim eq {full}
@nolog melee\.charge

# 5. Either factor alone keeps a swing low: the speed range out of reach (a fast swing too slow for it), then the size
# range out of reach (a fast swing too small for it) - both the minimum
playground kill
@until playground.npcAlive eq false 5s
playground pull respawn
@until playground.npcAlive eq true 5s
playground place 60
melee slash dagger 0 0 15 19
@until vr.melee.params.slash.speedMin eq 15 5s
@until vr.melee.recovery.left eq 0 5s
@remember hits vr.melee.hits
vr-sim @+1-8 hand right pos 0.45 -0.8 -0.35
@until vr.melee.hits ge {hits+1} 5s
@until vr.melee.swinging eq false 5s
@assert vr.melee.last.swing gt 0
@assert vr.melee.last.aim eq 0.1
melee slash dagger 2 3 0 0
@until vr.melee.params.slash.pathMin eq 2 5s
@until vr.melee.recovery.left eq 0 5s
@remember hits vr.melee.hits
vr-sim @+1-8 hand right pos -0.4 -0.8 -0.35
@until vr.melee.hits ge {hits+1} 5s
@until vr.melee.swinging eq false 5s
@assert vr.melee.last.swing gt 0
@assert vr.melee.last.speed gt 4.5
@assert vr.melee.last.aim eq 0.1
melee slash dagger default

# 6. A fast lunge along the blade (8 m/s, the lunge range set to always full): the full damage, kind thrust. The hand
# drawn back and to the middle slowly first
playground kill
@until playground.npcAlive eq false 5s
playground pull respawn
@until playground.npcAlive eq true 5s
playground place 60
melee stab dagger 0 0 2 4.5
@until vr.melee.params.stab.pathMax eq 0 5s
vr-sim @+1-40 hand right pos 0.45 -0.8 0.1; vr-sim @+41-80 hand right pos 0 -0.8 0.1
@frames 95
@until vr.melee.recovery.left eq 0 5s
@remember swings vr.melee.swings
@remember hits vr.melee.hits
@mark
vr-sim @+1-5 hand right pos 0 -0.8 -0.35
@until vr.melee.swings ge {swings+1} 5s
@until vr.melee.swinging eq false 5s
@assert vr.melee.hits ge {hits+1}
@assert vr.melee.last.kind eq thrust
@assert vr.melee.last.aim ge 0.99
@log melee\.hit source=player target=goblin_base_\d+ .*aim=1\.00 speed=\S+ size=\S+ kind=thrust
melee stab dagger default

# 7. The goblin fighting the player: a touch of the slowly swept dagger deals the minimum - a touch, no swing hit. The
# set-up: the mode lever (aggressive: the goblin's script takes the hits), then its fight behaviour and target set
# directly (playground fight) - the playground's goblin did not reach both on its own within 15 s, the save's goblin
# of melee-swing does after a hit
vr-sim @+1-40 hand right pos 0.45 -0.8 -0.35
@frames 50
playground pull mode
@until playground.npcMode eq aggressive 5s
playground fight
@until playground.npcFighting eq true 5s
playground place 60
@frames 60
# Still fighting the player, still in reach of the sweep
@assert playground.npcFightBehaviour eq true
@assert playground.npcTargetsPlayer eq true
@assert playground.npcDistance lt 100
@remember touches vr.melee.touches
@remember hits vr.melee.hits
@mark
vr-sim @+1-60 hand right pos -0.4 -0.8 -0.35
@until vr.melee.touches ge {touches+1} 5s
@frames 10
@assert vr.melee.hits eq {hits}
@assert vr.melee.last.swing eq 0
@assert vr.melee.last.aim eq 0.1
@log melee\.hit source=player target=goblin_base_\d+ weapon=\S+ damage=\S+ aim=0\.10 speed=\S+ size=\S+ kind=\S+

# 8. vr_melee_noswing=none (set live): a touch deals nothing, also to the fighting goblin (whose own strikes on the
# player are source=goblin...)
melee noswing none
@until vr.melee.params.noSwing eq none 5s
vr-sim @+1-60 hand right pos 0.45 -0.8 -0.35
@frames 75
playground place 60
@remember touches vr.melee.touches
@mark
vr-sim @+1-60 hand right pos -0.4 -0.8 -0.35
@frames 75
@assert vr.melee.touches eq {touches}
@nolog melee\.hit source=player
melee noswing min
@until vr.melee.params.noSwing eq min 5s
playground pull mode
@until playground.npcMode eq peaceful 5s

# 9. A resting blade touches no world geometry - no wall sound, no durability (the engine's isHit stays false) - while
# a swing into the wall still strikes it, once: the player at the respawn lever's wall, the dagger held into the wall
# slowly, then swept along it
approach lever_9002
@frames 10
approach lever_9002
@frames 30
vr-sim head rot 0 0 0
vr-sim @+1-60 hand right pos 0.25 -0.35 -0.6
@frames 90
@assert vr.melee.swinging eq false
@assert vr.melee.worldHit eq false
@remember swings vr.melee.swings
vr-sim @+1-8 hand right pos -0.35 -0.35 -0.6
@until vr.melee.swings ge {swings+1} 5s
@until vr.melee.swinging eq false 5s
@assert vr.melee.worldHit eq true

@assert errors eq 0
